pageType: content
notes: |
  Tritium and first-wall materials bottleneck slide. Analyzes the global civilian tritium supply cliff, pointing out that peak inventories (~25–30 kg in CANDU reactors) decay at 5.5% annually and will drop below 10 kg by 2035 as reactors retire. Proves that DT commercial plants must achieve TBR of 1.05 to 1.15. In parallel, evaluates 14.1 MeV neutron damage on first-wall steels (10–15 dpa/year), helium embrittlement, and the critical lack of an operational 14 MeV material irradiation test facility.
